<title>USA: Brazil files $5 billion debt shelf with U.S. SEC.</title>
<headline>Brazil files $5 billion debt shelf with U.S. SEC.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil filed Wednesday a shelf registration with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $5 billion in debt securities.</p>
<p>The debt securities may be issued in the form of bonds, debentures and/or notes, the filing said.</p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used for general purposes of the government, including refinancing of domestic and external debt.</p>
</text>
